  "description": "We've taken the demands of children's bikes seriously, distilling our own experience from the gravity sector and adding just the right amount of it. The contact points with the bike – pedals & cranks, handlebars & grips, and the saddle – were developed in collaboration with Sixpack specifically for the ergonomics of little shredders. The sophisticated geometry and Sixpack 1st Ride components ensure optimal control and therefore safety on every ride. The compact frame, combined with the relatively large 16-inch wheels, ensures the necessary smoothness, making it feel like a familiar environment for the kids. The first turns of the crank are effortless, and the hydraulic disc brakes enable safe braking with minimal effort – adapted to small hands. The Barney is ideal for children between 95 cm and 115 cm. With the Barney, nothing stands in the way of their first real bike ride.",
